title: Analytics › Case list panel
route: /analytics
intro: The cases behind one number. The same rows were counted to make the number, so the count in the panel always equals the number you clicked. Opened from a headline figure, a month on the trend, a grid cell, a reason, a scorecard count, a length of stay row, a process month or a site cell.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click any number on the page"
overlay o1 "Panel: the title says what was clicked, for example 'Cardinal: Opioid use disorder'\nSubtitle: '131 cases · This quarter · Both sites', plus the filters in force\nButton 'Copy summary'"
screen a1 "Three counts: 'Approved as requested', 'Approved in part', 'Denied'\n'Most common reasons' when there are denials\nThe cases table with outcome tabs, sorting and paging"
click c1 "Click a case row"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Case summary panel"
decision q1 "Is it one payer's reason?"
click c2 "Click 'Open in Denial Intelligence' (footer)"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Open denials list"
click b1 "Click 'Copy summary'"
process b2 "Copies the title, count, outcome counts and top reasons\nToast 'List summary copied'"
input k1 "Press Escape"
process k2 "Closes the top panel only\nFocus goes back to what was clicked"
decision q2 "Opened on top of a payer panel?"
screen e1 "The payer panel shows again"
end e2 "Back on the page"

s1 --> o1 --> a1
a1 --> c1 --> g1
o1 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| c2 --> g2
q1 -->|No| a1
o1 --> b1 --> b2
o1 --> k1 --> k2 --> q2
q2 -->|Yes| e1
q2 -->|No| e2
